{"abstract":[{"text":"The algebraic connectivity λ₂: the second smallest eigenvalue of the Laplacian L (of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"normalized Laplacian N with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"normalized"},{"text":"), 0 exactly when the graph is not connected (a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"weight-0 edge does not connect). NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"algebraic_connectivity"},{"text":"; Fiedler 1973.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/algebraicConnectivity(normalized:tolerance:maxIterations:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"algebraicConnectivity","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"normalized","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":"?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"SpectralGraphTheory"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"FiedlerVector.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpectralGraphTheory\/FiedlerVector.swift#L88"},"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE21algebraicConnectivity10normalized9tolerance13maxIterationsSdSb_SdSiSgtAA13NoConvergenceVYKF","title":"algebraicConnectivity(normalized:tolerance:maxIterations:)"},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/algebraicconnectivity(normalized:tolerance:maxiterations:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"algebraicConnectivity","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"normalized","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":" = false, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"text":" = 1e-8, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization, the null space projected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, from a fixed start vector: on σI − L (σ twice the largest weighted degree; 2I − N with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"normalized"},{"type":"text","text":") while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on L⁺ by shift-invert, each product a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz pair is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accepted when its residual is at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"type":"text","text":" · λ₂, so λ₂ is relative to itself however"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the weights spread; the value is then the vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dense solver below 64 vertices. O((n + m) · products) time; 31 n "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s (34 n from 5,000"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, for the polynomial filter), and on the shift-invert path O(n + m) more for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"solver."}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"At least two vertices, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at least 1."}]}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Throws","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":" when the Lanczos run on L⁺ spends "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":" matrix–vector"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"products (1,000 when nil) without converging, with the products spent and the Ritz"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"residual relative to 1\/λ₂. The run on σI − L that may come first hands over to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 + 20√n products or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whichever is smaller. Each shift-invert product is a conjugate-gradient solve that throws,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with its own iterations and relative residual, after 20,000 + 2n. Below 64 vertices the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dense solver answers and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":" is unused. Only a tolerance below rounding has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reached the default limits in the measurements."}]}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"references":{"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols","abstract":[],"title":"GraphProtocols"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"abstract":[],"title":"Graph"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory","role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"SpectralGraphTheory","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/NoConvergence":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/noconvergence","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NoConvergence","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The error an iterative method throws when it spends its iteration limit without meeting its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stopping rule: a power iteration (eigenvector and Katz centrality, PageRank, HITS), a Lanczos"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or conjugate-gradient run, or a QL eigenvalue iteration. Named after Eigen’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ComputationInfo::NoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":"; NetworkX raises "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PowerIterationFailedConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":" and SciPy"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ArpackNoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":" in the same place."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","title":"NoConvergence"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols/Graph/algebraicConnectivity(normalized:tolerance:maxIterations:)":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/algebraicconnectivity(normalized:tolerance:maxiterations:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"algebraicConnectivity"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"normalized"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tolerance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maxIterations"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"NoConvergence"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double"}],"type":"topic","title":"algebraicConnectivity(normalized:tolerance:maxIterations:)","abstract":[{"text":"The algebraic connectivity λ₂: the second smallest eigenvalue of the Laplacian L (of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"normalized Laplacian N with ","type":"text"},{"code":"normalized","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), 0 exactly when the graph is not connected (a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"weight-0 edge does not connect). NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"code":"algebraic_connectivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; Fiedler 1973.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/algebraicConnectivity(normalized:tolerance:maxIterations:)"}}}